From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: core: Ignore userspace keepalives once the system
 goes down

A watchdog that keeps running through a reboot is there to reset a
system whose reboot hangs. But userspace still runs after reboot(2) is
called: a watchdog daemon that was not stopped first (systemd after
"systemctl reboot --force --force") keeps pinging, so a hang in
device_shutdown() is never ended.

Ignore userspace keepalives once system_state is past SYSTEM_RUNNING.
da9062_wdt and da9063_wdt do the same in their ping handlers since
commit 2f61b3a74699 ("watchdog: da9062: da9063: prevent pings ahead of
machine reset").

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
index d789500..34cc3c3 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
@@ -195,6 +195,10 @@ static int watchdog_ping(struct watchdog_device *wdd)
 	if (!watchdog_hw_running(wdd))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Userspace still runs during a reboot that hangs in the kernel */
+	if (system_state > SYSTEM_RUNNING)
+		return 0;
+
 	set_bit(_WDOG_KEEPALIVE, &wd_data->status);
 
 	wd_data->last_keepalive = ktime_get();
-- 
